---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout pageId="pathway">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container page-hero__grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Oberlin 3-2 guide</span><h1>Planning the 3-2 pathway.</h1><p class="page-hero__lead">Oberlin describes a route that begins with three years of liberal-arts study and continues at an affiliated engineering school. Each partner sets its own prerequisites, application rules, costs, and degree structure.</p><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="https://www.oberlin.edu/aarc/advising-guides-major/3-2-engineering-program" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Oberlin’s official guide ↗</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="#planning">View planning steps</a></div></div>
    <div class="page-hero__side"><figure class="page-hero__figure"><img src="assets/images/photos/circuit-board-blue.jpg" width="1200" height="960" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="A blue circuit board photographed close up"></figure><aside class="page-hero__aside"><strong>Partner programs differ</strong><p>Compare the program length, degrees, prerequisites, admission process, housing, and financial aid for each school.</p><p class="callout callout--warning"><strong>Compare the full cost.</strong><br>Include tuition, aid, housing, travel, and the number of semesters required.</p></aside></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="planning">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Planning timeline</span><h2>Begin with the course sequence.</h2></div><p>Map Oberlin’s math and science sequence against the prerequisites for the engineering field and partner school you are considering.</p></div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__period">Before or during year 1</div><div><h3>Start the math and science sequence</h3><p>Discuss placement, calculus, physics, chemistry, computer science, and possible engineering fields with an adviser.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> Which courses must be taken in sequence, and what happens if one is delayed?</p></div></article>
      <article class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__period">Year 1 to year 2</div><div><h3>Compare partner requirements</h3><p>Build a table for each partner covering prerequisites, grade expectations, application dates, financial-aid processes, and degree options.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> Which requirements apply to my intended major and entry year?</p></div></article>
      <article class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__period">Year 2</div><div><h3>Check the whole Oberlin degree</h3><p>Review major, distribution, writing, residence, and other graduation requirements instead of looking only at engineering prerequisites.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> What must be completed before leaving Oberlin, and what may be completed through transfer credit?</p></div></article>
      <article class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__period">Year 2 to year 3</div><div><h3>Plan the application and transition</h3><p>Confirm application materials, recommendations, transcripts, housing, transportation, visa implications where relevant, and financial aid.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> What deadlines are controlled by Oberlin, and which are controlled by the partner school?</p></div></article>
      <article class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__period">Year 3</div><div><h3>Finalize the degree and application plan</h3><p>Before leaving Oberlin, confirm the course record, remaining degree requirements, admission status, aid package, and transfer-credit decisions.</p><p><strong>Ask:</strong> Who should I contact when a requirement or transfer decision is unclear?</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--soft">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Affiliated institutions</span><h2>Compare each partner separately.</h2></div><p>Each card links to the partner’s program page. Check the rules for the year you expect to apply.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-grid" data-partner-grid aria-live="polite"><div class="empty-state"><h3>Loading partner information…</h3><p>Preparing partner-school links.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container split">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Advising meeting checklist</span><h2>Bring specific questions.</h2><ul class="check-list"><li>My intended Oberlin major and possible engineering field</li><li>My current math and science placement</li><li>A draft course plan for the full route</li><li>Partner prerequisites I have checked</li><li>Questions about financial aid and total cost</li><li>Questions about housing, credit transfer, and degree timing</li><li>Backup options if I change fields or stay four years at Oberlin</li></ul></div>
    <aside class="form-shell"><h3>After an advising meeting</h3><p>Record who you spoke with, what was confirmed, the source link, and any unresolved questions.</p></aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--maroon">
  <div class="container split split--center"><div><span class="eyebrow">Student discussion</span><h2>Talk with other students considering 3-2.</h2><p>Submit membership interest if you want to compare course plans, partner schools, costs, or engineering fields with other Oberlin students.</p></div><div class="page-hero__actions"><a class="button button--secondary" href="join">Submit membership interest</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="contact">Contact the society</a></div></div>
</section>
</Layout>
